 for id in the arry products\r\n\r\n\r\n## 🔬 Minimal Reproduction\r\n\r\n### What's the affected URL?**\r\n<!-- ✍️edit:-->\r\nhttps://angular.io/start/start-routing\r\n\r\n### Reproduction Steps**\r\n<!-- If applicable please list the steps to take to reproduce the issue -->\r\n<!-- ✍️edit:-->\r\nIf you followed the steps of the first tutorial and this tutorial https://angular.io/start/start-routing the products in the array product have **no Id**\r\n\r\n### Expected vs Actual Behavior**\r\n<!-- If applicable please describe the difference between the expected and actual behavior after following the repro steps. -->\r\n<!-- ✍️edit:-->\r\nThe url should show: `../products/{id}` but as there is no id it shows `../products/undefined` and also the product details are not shown, because of that.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## 📷Screenshot\r\n<!-- Often a screenshot can help to capture the issue better than a long description. -->\r\n<!-- ✍️upload a screenshot:-->\r\nproduct.ts\r\n![grafik](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/71433252/102608972-0a787e00-412b-11eb-853f-24bedb2f7d07.png)\r\n\r\nresults in\r\n![grafik](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/71433252/102609282-7f4bb800-412b-11eb-9a26-8c36c13bf97b.png)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## ✍️Solution\r\nChange code to this in products.ts to fix the guide\r\n<pre><code>\r\nexport const products = [\r\n  //added id's for fix\r\n  {\r\n    id: 1,\r\n    name: \"Phone XL\",\r\n    price: 799,\r\n    description: \"A large phone with one of the best screens\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    id: 2,\r\n    name: \"Phone Mini\",\r\n    price: 699,\r\n    description: \"A great phone with one of the best cameras\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    id: 3,\r\n    name: \"Phone Standard\",\r\n    price: 299,\r\n    description: \"\"\r\n  }\r\n];\r\n[</code></pre>]\r\n\r\nedited: links","closed_by":{"login":"atscott","id":479713,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTcxMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https:/